cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite ggml.
title: ggml tensor library (vendored)
abstract: >-
  ggml, the tensor library, from the org's fork, added here as a squashed git
  subtree at vendor/ggml. The guest ELFs build it static for riscv64 at
  rv64gc with one thread and no dynamic backend loading (GGML_NATIVE,
  GGML_BACKEND_DL, GGML_OPENMP, GGML_LLAMAFILE, GGML_RVV, GGML_RV_ZFH,
  GGML_RV_ZVFH, GGML_RV_ZICBOP, GGML_RV_ZIHINTPAUSE and GGML_RV_ZVFBFWMA off;
  __riscv_v_intrinsic undefined for ggml-cpu, Gate 0F finding 5). ggml-cpu is
  the in-guest reference; guest/ggml-rd is the GPU backend, over Godot's
  RenderingDevice, with kernels generated from lean/Ggml. Adapted here, in
  tests/test-backend-ops.cpp only, both marked "interactor-dress-on": (1)
  N_THREADS is wrapped in #ifndef so an embedder can set it (the guest builds
  with -DN_THREADS=1; its threads are serialized, Gate 0C); (2) under
  GGML_GUEST_REGISTER_BACKENDS, main() calls the embedder's
  ggml_guest_register_backends() instead of ggml_backend_load_all(). The
  guest also compiles the file with -Dmain=... and links it with
  --wrap=ggml_backend_init_by_type (guest/ggml_test), which changes no
  source. Nothing else is modified.
type: software
authors:
